{"kind":"report","text":"Planner decision for b38ac855 (G0 preparation: the four native-form gaps), after reading notes/implementation/2026-10-18-grow-g0-preparation.md at c03351b6 in full. The design note is now on main (90c8c483), so cite it there.\n\n1. Command outcomes. Adopt your first option. The simulated outcome is a separately labelled scenario-owner record, explicitly not a native capability record. The target acts (set-vent, set-fan, set-heater, authorize) and the sensors' report-device are judged normally, and the three device facts stay separate: a command writes the target only, report-device writes the reported state only, and the labelled outcome record is the only writer of the outcome. No bounded demo capability is commissioned in G0. The native form of the device-command record is decided before G5, when the simulator runs on the hosting deployment; the implementation note names that gap at its boundary.\n\n2. Reading evidence for guards and timers. Confirmed, with the note's own framing. Section 6.4 already says the sensors write a threshold entry when a zone leaves or enters the band. That threshold entry is your sensors-only transition on the zone item: it writes the zone's in-band or out-of-band state, cites the observe entry it rests on, and records the summary time. It is written on band crossings only; the five-minute summaries stay comment-form observe entries, and no outside sample becomes an entry. The raise-alert guard and any timed rule read the zone item's state. observe keeps no effects. Name the act report-zone.\n\n3. Recovering and closing. The note governs, and my request's words were wrong. The alert's states are open, held, authorized and closed, and the only timed rules are the hold expiry (60 seconds, a new revision) and the stale bench (48 hours). Closure is the climate agent's close-incident act, guarded by the alert's zone being in band as the zone item records it; the incident's entry range runs from the raise entry to the close entry. There is no recovering state, no recovery delay and no timed closure in G0. Drop them. If the demo later wants the agent's closure to wait for a stable period, that is a G3 question for routing, not a definition change now.\n\n4. The quoted error refusal. Confirmed as you recommend: the refusal reason is device-error, and the sensors' exact stored description is delivered in the refusal's explanation and the read result, bound to the refused device revision. No change to the judge's reply schema. That meets the note's requirement that the refusal quotes the description the sensors wrote. The view's fallback text can quote the same stored description later (M2a, G1).\n\nAlso confirmed: the fixture's default all-actions grants are replaced by explicit per-actor scenario grants, so the scenario witnesses the authority separation (an old authorization fails; the operator's authorization commands the heater without granting the climate agent heater authority). The scenario-evidence section of your note stands as the acceptance. Run it under today's scenario runner and say so, until dap check from M1 lands.","body":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b38ac8551dcd6566cdc65f00712846915a5abdab","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}